Forest Inventory Analysis System
An interactive web platform developed in R (Shiny) for the automation, processing, and analysis of forest inventory and phytosociological data. The tool was designed to meet the technical requirements for environmental licensing and vegetation clearing, offering support ranging from sampling statistics to geospatial data export.

Developed by Heitor C. Lacerda to meet the operational routines and methodological requirements of Grupo G5S Projetos e Consultoria.

✨ Key Features
The system was built to handle the high complexity and variability of native forest fragments, supporting three distinct sampling designs:

Census (100%): Complete survey of the intervention area (ideal for the removal of isolated individuals).

Simple Random Sampling: For continuous and homogeneous fragments.

Stratified Sampling: For heterogeneous areas subdivided into successional stages or phytophysiognomies.

⚙️ Integrated Analytical Capabilities
Corrective Extrapolation (Reference Inventory): A module dedicated to areas subject to regulatory enforcement actions. The system automatically calculates the Extrapolation Factor, projecting the volume and individual count from the physically sampled area to the total extent of the intervention.

Volumetric Calculations: Equation based on the CETEC Model for the local biome, with parametric definition of the Stacking Factor for conversion into steres (st).

Horizontal and Vertical Phytosociology: Automated calculation of Density, Dominance, and Frequency (Absolute and Relative), Importance Value Index (IVI and IVIAmp), Coverage Value (VC), and Sociological Position (PSR) across three height strata.

Successional Dynamics and Yield: Automatic grouping into diameter classes (inverted J-curve) with separation of individuals vs. ...stems and calculation of wood yield by multiproduct categories (DBH < 15, 15–30, 30–45, > 45 cm).

Sampling Statistics: Rigorous calculation of variance, standard error, coefficient of variation, sampling error, and sample sufficiency (based on an allowable error of 10%).

Ecological Analyses: Instant generation of diversity indices (Shannon-Weaver, Simpson, Pielou, Jentsch Quotient), plus screening for protected species or those exempt from logging.

Mapping and GIS: Intelligent coordinate conversion (DMS or Decimal Degrees) with interactive map rendering (Leaflet) and native export to Shapefile (.shp) and KML formats.

🛠️ Prerequisites and Installation
The platform was developed in R. To run it locally, you need to have R and RStudio installed, along with the following libraries:

R
# Installation of required packages
pacotes <- c("shiny", "tidyverse", "DT", "leaflet", "plotly",
"sf", "zip", "bslib", "shinycssloaders")

instalados <- pacotes %in% rownames(installed.packages())
if(any(!instalados)) install.packages(pacotes[!instalados])
